<h2>What it is for</h2>
<p>Leave and absence records who is away, asks a manager to decide leave, keeps annual leave allowances and shows a team calendar. It is not payroll: Care Core does not pay anyone, work out sick pay or know your bank holidays.</p>
<p>Everyone with a login linked to a person sees <strong>Leave</strong>. Managers and administrators also have <strong>Team leave</strong>. It is part of the Staff module (<a href="/docs/admin-modules">Modules</a>).</p>

<h2>Asking for leave</h2>
<h2>Swapping annual leave with a colleague</h2>
<p>Choose <strong>Swap annual leave with a colleague</strong> on the Leave page. You pick one of your approved annual leave spells that has not started and one of a colleague's. The two must be the same number of working days, so nobody's allowance changes, and neither person may have other leave on the dates they would take. The colleague agrees, then a manager who is neither of the two decides. On approval the two leave records exchange dates, and Care Core tells other systems (for example Rota Core) the new dates. Nothing changes before then, and a swap that is refused, declined or withdrawn changes nothing.</p>
<p>Under <strong>Leave</strong>, choose what for (annual leave, other paid leave or unpaid leave), the first and last day, and whether either end is a half day. The request goes to the managers. You can cancel it while it waits, and cancel approved leave that has not started yet. Once leave has started, only a manager can cancel it.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Days</strong> are working days, Monday to Friday, with half days counting as half. <strong>Bank holidays are not taken off</strong>: Care Core does not guess a calendar. The manager who approves can type the right number of days.</li>
<li>You cannot book leave on days that already have leave or absence booked, and leave cannot start in the past: ask a manager to record leave that has already happened.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Deciding</h2>
<p>On <strong>Team leave</strong>, each waiting request has <strong>Approve</strong> and <strong>Decline</strong>. Declining needs a note so the person knows why. <strong>Nobody decides their own request</strong>: it waits for another manager. Any manager can decide any request: Care Core does not limit it to a line manager.</p>

<h2>Sickness</h2>
<p>A person (or a manager for them) records sickness from the first day off. It needs no approval, and the last day can be left empty while they are still off. A manager sees open sickness under <strong>Still off sick</strong> and closes it with the last day off, or the person presses <strong>I am back</strong>.</p>
<p>Closing sickness raises a task for a manager, <em>Return-to-work conversation</em>. After the conversation, press <strong>Held today</strong> on Team leave and record it as an appraisal of type return to work under <a href="/docs/compliance">Registrations, supervision and learning</a>. Care Core does not decide what counts as too much sickness: it shows, for each person, how many separate absences and how many working days in the last 12 months, as facts for a conversation.</p>
<p>Sickness is health information. Managers can see the kind of absence and any note; other staff cannot. Events and webhooks about absence leave out the kind (see the <a href="/docs/event-catalogue">event catalogue</a>).</p>

<h2>Allowances and the leave year</h2>
<p>Under <strong>Allowances and sickness</strong> on Team leave, choose the month the leave year starts (January unless you change it) and set each person’s allowance in days, in halves. Part-time allowances are entered pro rata: Care Core does not work them out. The person sees their allowance, what is approved, what is waiting and what is left. Only annual leave uses the allowance. Leave that straddles two leave years counts in each year only for the days inside it. Carrying leave over to the next year is not done by Care Core: set next year’s allowance to include it.</p>

<h2>The team calendar</h2>
<p>The calendar shows a month, for everyone or one team: one row per person, one column per day, <strong>A</strong> annual leave, <strong>S</strong> sickness, <strong>O</strong> other paid, <strong>U</strong> unpaid and <strong>?</strong> for a request still waiting. Weekends are shaded. <strong>Away today</strong> lists everyone approved to be away now.</p>

<h2>Recording on someone’s behalf</h2>
<p>A manager can record leave or sickness for anyone, including dates in the past. It is recorded as approved straight away and appears in the log.</p>
